# Respect/Validation -- the only project here whose suite is a full `composer qa`:
# seven steps, two runners, a linter, a static analyser and two console commands.
# Pinned to a commit rather than a tag: the tree tracks `main`.
REPO="https://github.com/Respect/Validation.git"
REF="b885ab8"
# phpcs sniffs 711 files and is by far the most expensive step here: ~9s under php, ~86s
# under phl. It used to be ~14 MINUTES, and the reason recorded here was wrong twice -- it
# was not "real work" in phpdoc-parser's MARK alternation, it was a leaked `foreach` step
# making OP_FOREACH_INIT quadratic, and then it was the reference table's rehash (both
# fixed 26 Aug 2026; see DONE.md). Its MEMORY was the same story: 4205 MB against php's
# 102 until the closure leak behind it was found, 283 MB now. The budget stays: it is per
# STEP and both engines get it, so a timeout is a comparable answer rather than a hang,
# and this is the step an engine performance regression would show up in first.
STEP_TIMEOUT=1800
